Exif parsing library written in pure Rust
-----------------------------------------

   This is a pure-Rust library to parse Exif data.
   This library parses Exif attributes in a raw Exif data block.
   It can also read Exif data directly from some image formats.

   Supported formats are:
   -  TIFF and some RAW image formats based on it
   -  JPEG
   -  HEIF and coding-specific variations including HEIC and AVIF
   -  PNG
   -  WebP

Usage
-----

   Add a dependency entry to your Cargo.toml.  Specify "kamadak-exif"
   if you use crates.io.  The canonical name of this crate is "exif",
   but it is renamed on crates.io to avoid a naming conflict.

      [dependencies]
      kamadak-exif = "x.y.z"

   Add the following to your crate root (before Rust 2018).

      extern crate exif;

   Run "cargo doc" in the source directory to generate the API reference.
   It is also available online at <https://docs.rs/kamadak-exif>.

   See examples directory for sample codes.

TIFF SubIFDs
------------

   The experimental Exif::sub_ifds(parent) accessor reads the direct
   SubIFDs referenced by a top-level IFD as separate field collections.
   Existing fields() and get_field() results remain unchanged: an IFD0
   preview is not replaced by a RAW image stored in a SubIFD.
   Callers must distinguish the images using their TIFF metadata; neither
   the first image nor the largest dimensions universally identify a
   primary image.

HEIF primary image dimensions (fork extension)
----------------------------------------------

   experimental::get_heif_primary_image_dimensions reads the stored
   spatial extent associated with the primary HEIF item. This is container
   metadata, not a synthesized Exif field. Rotation and cropping are not
   applied. The reader must be positioned at the start of the file.

RAW containers and camera identity (fork extensions)
----------------------------------------------------

   Reader::read_from_container also extracts embedded EXIF from Minolta
   MRW (TTW), Fujifilm RAF (JPEG), Panasonic RW2 (JPEG), and Olympus ORF
   TIFF directories. RAF/RW2 EXIF dimensions describe the preview, not
   necessarily the raw sensor. Use experimental::read_raw_dimensions
   separately for recorded full/cropped RAF or RW2 sensor extents.

   ARI, CR3, CRW and Kyocera RAW do not use that Reader entry point:

      let ari = exif::experimental::read_ari_metadata(&mut reader)?;
      // ARI camera model and stored image dimensions only; no capture date.

      let cr3 = exif::experimental::read_cr3_metadata(&mut reader)?;
      let id = cr3.image_unique_id()?;
      // cr3.fields contains standard TIFF, EXIF and GPS fields.
      // cr3.maker_notes retains the independent Canon CMT3 TIFF bytes.

      let legacy = exif::experimental::read_legacy_raw_metadata(&mut reader)?;
      // CIFF (CRW): camera, timestamp, valid timezone, image dimensions.
      // Kyocera: camera and local capture-time text from its native header.

   CR3 follows the declared Canon UUID/CMT boxes. CMT2 and CMT4 are parsed
   in their EXIF and GPS namespaces, including their pointer directories.
   Legacy native values remain separate from EXIF tags; the CIFF numeric
   timestamp does not by itself establish a UTC instant.

   Exif::image_unique_id(In::PRIMARY) prefers standard ImageUniqueID and
   otherwise reads supported Canon/Apple MakerNotes. CR3's corresponding
   method reads standard EXIF first, then Canon CMT3. Other MakerNotes are
   not interpreted as identity sources. These APIs are read-only and do
   not imply full vendor metadata, RAW pixel decoding, or universal RAW
   format support. Missing metadata returns None/NotFound; malformed
   recognized structures return an error.

Dependencies
------------

   Rust 1.60 or later is required to build.

Standards
---------

   -  Exif Version 2.32
   -  DCF Version 2.0 (Edition 2010)
   -  TIFF Revision 6.0
   -  ISO/IEC 14496-12:2015
   -  ISO/IEC 23008-12:2017
   -  PNG Specification, Version 1.2
   -  Extensions to the PNG 1.2 Specification, version 1.5.0
   -  WebP Container Specification, committed on 2018-04-20
